# Private keys are generated on first run and must never be committed.
# A repository that has held a private key must be treated as having
# published it -- rotating is the only fix, so the cheap defence is here.
keys/
*.pem

# Runtime output: the Cloud's store, photographs, exports, demo runs, and
# the raw launch logs run_sim.sh keeps so the filtered view is never the
# only copy of what happened.
store/
demo_run/
logs/
*.db

# GENERATED, and deliberately not tracked.
#
# These were committed once, while the README told you to regenerate them.
# Both cannot be right, and the way it failed is why they are here now: a
# regenerated world is a locally-modified tracked file, so the next
# `git pull` aborts -- and a pasted block of commands carries on past the
# abort, because each line of a paste runs independently. That left a
# demonstration running four commits behind, showing green spheres,
# with nothing on screen saying so.
#
# run_sim.sh now builds them (agri/world/ensure.py), so a fresh clone needs
# no extra step and a stale world cannot survive a pull.
worlds/
urdf/

# Python
__pycache__/
*.egg-info/
build/
dist/
